1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:02,800
OK, everybody.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:06,250
I want to welcome Harry and his daughter Michelle

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:07,790
to Thanksgiving with us.

4
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:08,950
Thank you, Dr. Stewart.

5
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:09,750
Call me Philip.

6
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:10,770
OK.

7
00:00:10,770 --> 00:00:13,130
But first, I think we should take a moment

8
00:00:13,130 --> 00:00:15,700
and remember the meaning of Thanksgiving.

9
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,370
Philip, I took Michelle to a school play

10
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:19,910
about the first Thanksgiving.

11
00:00:19,910 --> 00:00:22,430
Well, why don't you tell us about that, Michelle?

12
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:24,500
Thanksgiving was about the Pilgrims,

13
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,170
the first settlers in America.

14
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:28,490
They shared the first harvest with the Indians

15
00:00:28,490 --> 00:00:30,410
and gave thanks.

16
00:00:30,410 --> 00:00:31,400
All right.

17
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,880
Then in that spirit let each of us give thanks.

18
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,790
Each in his own way.

19
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:38,180
Who wants to begin?

20
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:40,490
I will.

21
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:45,120
I give thanks for being here with my family and for being well,

22
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,620
so I can enjoy you all.

23
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,040
All rihgt!

24
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,990
We love you, Grandpa.

25
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:57,400
I'd like to give thanks for a healthy year, a good job,

26
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,430
and for meeting Harry and Michelle.

27
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,820
We'd like to give thanks for meeting Susan

28
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,080
and the Stewart family.

29
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:06,420
I love you, Daddy.

30
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:07,230
Thanks, Harry.

31
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:08,760
That was very kind of you.

32
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:12,410
I'd like to give thanks for Grandpa coming to live with us.

33
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:14,830
And I'd also like to thank my math teacher

34
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:17,600
for giving me a passing grade.

35
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:21,310
And call me, Alexandra.

36
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:22,170
Oh, Robbie!

37
00:01:22,170 --> 00:01:24,140
She'll call.

38
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:25,950
You go first, Marilyn.

39
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:26,760
I'm thinking.

40
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:28,720
You go first.

41
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:34,790
Well, you all know I'm working on my photo album.

42
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:36,350
It's not finished yet.

43
00:01:36,350 --> 00:01:40,410
And I'd like to thank Marilyn for being so patient.

44
00:01:40,410 --> 00:01:42,060
Thanks, Richard.

45
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:44,170
I should thank you for encouraging me

46
00:01:44,170 --> 00:01:46,170
to keep working on my fashion designs.

47
00:01:46,170 --> 00:01:51,130
I'm lucky to have a husband with an artistic eye.

48
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:56,020
Oh, we have a lot to be thankful for.

49
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,920
For the food on this table.

50
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,670
Just like the Pilgrims.

51
00:01:59,670 --> 00:02:01,760
I'll go along with that, Ellen.

52
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:07,450
Well, help me serve, Robbie.

53
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:09,120
It was a wonderful meal, Mrs. Stewart.

54
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:09,920
Thank you.

55
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:11,840
And now to see the end of the football game.

56
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,690
Exactly.

57
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:15,330
Where are you going, Philip?

58
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:17,240
Remember, the Michigan football game?

59
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:20,080
And Michigan needs a touchdown.

60
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,560
Did you forget something?

61
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,490
Dad, your famous apple pie.

62
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:26,830
Just let me see the score, Ellen.

63
00:02:26,830 --> 00:02:27,920
Go ahead, Philip.

64
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:40,860
We should all take a little break before dessert.

65
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:44,500
Oh, who could that be?

66
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,850
Oh, it must be Alexandra.

67
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:48,980
I invited her to come by for dessert.

68
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:50,170
You did?

69
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:51,450
I like Ellen.

70
00:02:51,450 --> 00:02:52,960
You know everyone, Alexandra.

71
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:56,440
No, she doesn't know Harry Bennett and his daughter Michelle.

72
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,390
Nice to meet you.

73
00:02:57,390 --> 00:02:58,560
Hi.

74
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,200
Hello, Alexandra.

75
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,030
Hi, Marilyn.

76
00:03:01,030 --> 00:03:01,700
Hi, Susan.

77
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:02,980
Happy Thanksgiving.

78
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:05,600
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

79
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,200
Please sit down, Alexandra.

80
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:12,590
Dad, Richard--Alexandra's here.

81
00:03:12,590 --> 00:03:13,810
Michigan needs a touchdown.

82
00:03:13,810 --> 00:03:15,000
Three minutes to play.

83
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,630
Hi, Alexandra. Welcome.

84
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:17,820
Hello, Alexandra.

85
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:19,660
Yes, Michigan needs a touchdown.

86
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:22,850
One tiny little touchdown, with just three minutes to play.

87
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:24,650
You want Michigan to win.

88
00:03:24,650 --> 00:03:25,710
How'd you guess?

89
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:40,790
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

90
00:03:40,790 --> 00:03:42,460
What happened?

91
00:03:42,460 --> 00:03:45,380
We forgot to turn the oven on.

92
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:48,410
We did?

93
00:03:48,410 --> 00:03:50,280
Philip, why don't you go

94
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,390
watch the last three minutes of the game.

95
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:55,510
I will serve coffee and pumpkin pie.

96
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:59,110
OK. I'll be back in a few minutes.

97
00:03:59,110 --> 00:04:01,760
Robbie, would you bring the dessert plates.

98
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:03,950
And, Marilyn, would you pour coffee, please.

99
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:08,270
Sure, Ellen.

100
00:04:08,270 --> 00:04:10,740
How was your Thanksgiving dinner, Alexandra?

101
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:12,700
Just wonderful, Mr. Stewart.

102
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:14,550
The Molinas are a large family.

103
00:04:14,550 --> 00:04:16,420
I love being with them.

104
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,050
I'm glad you came by, Alexandra.

105
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:23,330
I am, too.

106
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:28,120
Touchdown! Touchdown! Touchdown!

107
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,920
Great Thanksgiving.

108
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:32,340
Lots to be thankful for.

109
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:34,760
Michigan scored a touchdown.

110
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:37,000
Alexandra came by.

111
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,440
And nobody misses Philip's famous apple pie.

112
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:44,440
Oh, Grandpa!
